# Help (i) icons + translations

When you add or materially change a **page**, **tab**, or major buyer/staff surface in `kaarobar-web` (and desktop/mobile mirrors where applicable):

## Supported locales (all required)

Ship help + UI strings for **every** locale in `LOCALES` (`kaarobar-web/lib/i18n/index.tsx`):

| Code | Language | Direction |
|------|----------|-----------|
| `en` | English | LTR |
| `ur` | Urdu | RTL |
| `de` | Deutsch | LTR |
| `pt-BR` | Português (Brasil) | LTR |
| `es` | Español | LTR |
| `fr` | Français | LTR |
| `ar` | العربية | RTL |

Do **not** ship English-only (or EN+UR-only) and leave the rest missing — missing catalog entries hide the (i) icon; missing message keys fall back to English and look unfinished.

Each app owns its locale catalogs — edit them directly (no shared locale package):
- Web: [`kaarobar-web/lib/i18n/messages/`](kaarobar-web/lib/i18n/messages/)
- Desktop: [`kaarobar-desktop/renderer/src/lib/i18n/messages/`](kaarobar-desktop/renderer/src/lib/i18n/messages/)
- Mobile / customer: their `lib/i18n/` catalogs
When the same chrome exists on multiple apps, update each app’s files in the same change.

## Info icon (required)

1. Pass `infoKey` on `PageHeader` and on each `TabBar` / `Tabs` item.
2. Add a matching topic in **all** help catalogs under [`kaarobar-web/lib/help/`](kaarobar-web/lib/help/):
   - `en.ts`, `ur.ts`, `de.ts`, `pt-BR.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, `ar.ts`
3. For staff features also used on desktop, mirror the **same keys** in [`kaarobar-desktop/renderer/src/lib/help/`](kaarobar-desktop/renderer/src/lib/help/) for every locale file above.
4. Key naming: `page.<area>` for pages, `tab.<area>.<tab>` for tabs (e.g. `page.market.discover`, `tab.settings.branding`).
5. Topic shape: `title`, `summary`, `what`, `how[]`, `when`, optional `tips[]`.
6. If `infoKey` is set but the catalog entry is missing for the active locale (and EN fallback is absent), the (i) icon **does not render** — always ship **all** locale catalogs + wire-up together.

Example:

```tsx
<PageHeader title={t("pages.fooTitle")} description={t("pages.fooDesc")} infoKey="page.foo" />
```

## Translations (required)

1. Add user-visible strings to **every** file under [`kaarobar-web/lib/i18n/messages/`](kaarobar-web/lib/i18n/messages/):
   - `en.json`, `ur.json`, `de.json`, `pt-BR.json`, `es.json`, `fr.json`, `ar.json`
2. Prefer `useT()` / `t("…")` over hardcoded English in UI chrome (titles, descriptions, empty states, primary CTAs).
3. Use `t("key", { count: n })` for interpolated strings.
4. When the same chrome exists on desktop/mobile/customer, update that app’s locale files too.
5. RTL: `ur` and `ar` use RTL layout — avoid hard-coded `left`/`right` in new UI; prefer logical CSS (`ms`/`me`, `start`/`end`).

## Do not skip

- New Settings / Marketing / Inventory tabs
- New consumer marketplace routes (Discover, catalog, checkout, etc.)
- Replacing a hardcoded title with i18n without adding `infoKey` when the surface is a full page/tab
- Adding a key only to `en`/`ur` while omitting `de` / `pt-BR` / `es` / `fr` / `ar`
